-- ============================================================
-- Warrior (Protection): Incite, redesigned again
-- ============================================================
-- "Incite (1, 1): Redesigned.  Your Heroic Strike, Thunder Clap and Cleave have
--  a chance equal to your shield block chance to do additional damage equal to
--  33/66/100% of your shield block value. (3 ranks)"
--
-- What it was: the Mocking Blow damage and cooldown package from
-- woa_2026_08_09_09.sql, with the cooldown half moved to C++ in
-- woa_2026_08_09_26.sql, plus a Revenge cooldown reset when a mocked enemy
-- attacked you.  All of it is retired below, including both scripts.
--
-- Why this shape.  The Revenge half was inert against exactly the targets that
-- mattered -- taunt does not land on players or boss-flagged creatures, so
-- there was no Mocking Blow aura to find -- and the rest of the talent was two
-- points of budget spent on a button Protection rarely presses.  This puts the
-- talent on the three abilities a Protection warrior actually spams and pays it
-- out of block value, the number the rest of the tree already scales (Toughness
-- feeds it, Shield Mastery multiplies it, Spellshield and Barricade convert it).
--
-- The proc rate is self-limiting by design: woa_2026_08_08_06.sql rebuilt Heroic
-- Strike and Cleave on the Cataclysm model -- instant, off the GCD, sharing a 3
-- second cooldown -- so those two together offer one opportunity per 3 seconds,
-- plus Thunder Clap.
--
-- Handled by DBC:
--   The per-rank percentage and the prose.  Effect1 is SPELL_AURA_DUMMY whose
--   base points carry 33/66/100 (32/65/99 + 1 die side), which is both what the
--   script reads and what $s1 prints.
--
--   The Mocking Blow modifier is removed by changing the aura TYPE, not by
--   zeroing its class mask.  woa_2026_08_09_26.sql records why that matters:
--   SpellInfo::IsAffected (SpellInfo.cpp:1333) treats an empty familyFlags as
--   "match everything", so a modifier with a cleared mask applies to the entire
--   class kit rather than to nothing.
--
--   The DBC class mask on Effect1 is left at 0 on purpose.  A DUMMY aura has no
--   modifier semantics, so a mask there would be inert decoration that reads as
--   though it were the filter.  The real filter is the spell_proc row.
--
-- Handled by C++ (modules/world_of_alonecraft/src/WarriorIncite.cpp,
-- spell_warr_incite):
--   The roll and the damage, neither of which the DBC can express.
--
-- Why a script at all.  Nothing in the game rolls one defensive chance to
-- decide whether an offensive ability procs, and no spell_proc column can refer
-- to a character stat -- Chance is a constant.  Block value is not a stat or a
-- rating either (Player::GetShieldBlockValue, Player.cpp:5115), so no aura can
-- read it as a damage source.  Spellshield (WarriorSpellshield.cpp) already
-- solves the identical problem from the defensive side and this reuses its
-- approach exactly.
--
-- Spells:
--   50685 / 50686 / 50687 = Incite ranks 1-3
--   200660                = the damage payload
--   694                   = Mocking Blow, whose script registration is dropped
-- ============================================================


